---
title: Bistek
servings: 4
course: dinner
cuisine: Filipino
tags: beef, dairy-free, fried, simmered
image: https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/4pqimk1683207418.jpg
source: https://panlasangpinoy.com/bistek-tagalog-beefsteak-recipe/
---

Marinate @beef{450%g} in @soy sauce{5%tbsp}, @lemon{1} (or calamansi), and ground black pepper for at least ~{1%hour}. Note: marinate overnight for best result.

Heat the @olive oil{4%tbsp} in a #frying pan{} then pan-fry half of the @onion{3} until the texture becomes soft. Set aside.

Drain the marinade from the beef. Set it aside. Pan-fry the beef on the same frying pan where the onions were fried for ~{1%minute} per side. Remove from the frying pan. Set aside.

Add more oil if needed. Saute @garlic{3%cloves} and remaining raw onions until onion softens.

Pour the remaining marinade and @water{240%ml}. Bring to a boil.

Add beef. Cover the frying pan and simmer until the meat is tender. Note: Add water as needed.

Season with ground black pepper and @salt{1%pinch} as needed. Top with pan-fried onions.

Transfer to a serving #plate{}. Serve hot. Share and Enjoy!
